WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.181 --> 00:00:19.832
The next morning The Lemonade Detectives discussed the mystery as they put the finishing touches on their float.

2
00:00:20.893 --> 00:00:24.855
"Let's list everything suspicious that's happened," Henry suggested.

3
00:00:24.875 --> 00:00:27.137
"Okay," Cole said.

4
00:00:27.157 --> 00:00:31.440
"The first thing we found out about was that threat on the website."

5
00:00:32.604 --> 00:00:33.885
"True," Henry said.

6
00:00:33.905 --> 00:00:37.268
"But that wasn't the first thing that happened.

7
00:00:38.189 --> 00:00:40.391
The threat appeared sometime yesterday.

8
00:00:41.311 --> 00:00:45.355
Mrs. Sweet's candy disappeared before that, on Thursday night."

9
00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:46.956
"Don't forget Mr.

10
00:00:47.016 --> 00:00:48.717
Fleming's threat," Maggie said.

11
00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:50.519
"That happened yesterday too."

12
00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:56.344
"So did Jackson's comment about the parade being cancelled," Henry finished.

13
00:00:56.364 --> 00:00:58.806
"So who are our suspects?"

14
00:00:59.927 --> 00:01:01.308
"Jackson," Cole said.

15
00:01:02.248 --> 00:01:07.070
"If your theory is right, he could be trying to create an interesting story to write about."

16
00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.351
"Yeah," Maggie said.

17
00:01:09.371 --> 00:01:12.072
"I think Snake is a better suspect, though."

18
00:01:12.092 --> 00:01:16.114
"Snake?" Henry had forgotten about the teenager.

19
00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:18.795
"Why?" Henry asked Maggie.

20
00:01:18.815 --> 00:01:21.836
"His band isn't even making a float anymore."

21
00:01:21.856 --> 00:01:24.277
"Exactly," Maggie said.

22
00:01:24.297 --> 00:01:27.999
"This stuff started happening after the band dropped out of the parade.

23
00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:30.900
Maybe Snake is mad about dropping out.

24
00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:34.269
And now he doesn't want anyone else to win those prizes either."

25
00:01:34.289 --> 00:01:36.791
"Maybe," Henry said.

26
00:01:36.811 --> 00:01:39.753
"I guess we should keep him on the list.

27
00:01:40.553 --> 00:01:42.114
Who else?"

28
00:01:42.174 --> 00:01:43.555
"Mr. Newman," Cole said.

29
00:01:43.575 --> 00:01:45.256
"What about him?"

30
00:01:45.476 --> 00:01:46.316
Maggie asked.

31
00:01:47.237 --> 00:01:48.097
Cole shrugged.

32
00:01:48.778 --> 00:01:49.518
"He was in Mrs.

33
00:01:49.598 --> 00:01:51.739
Sweet's shed the night her candy disappeared."

34
00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:54.301
"True," Henry said.

35
00:01:54.321 --> 00:01:58.323
"The rumor Jackson started and the threat from Mr.

36
00:01:58.403 --> 00:02:02.949
Fleming could be red herrings—false clues that are confusing us.

37
00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.191
Why do you think Mr.

38
00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.731
Newman should be a suspect?"

39
00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:10.794
"You said his daughter is in Snake's band," Cole said.

40
00:02:10.814 --> 00:02:12.455
"Maybe Mr.

41
00:02:12.555 --> 00:02:15.697
Newman wanted to sabotage other floats because of that."

42
00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:18.418
"Maybe," Henry said.

43
00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:24.221
"But he didn't seem very excited about the band when I heard him talking to Jade."

44
00:02:24.241 --> 00:02:26.723
"Yeah," Maggie agreed.

45
00:02:26.743 --> 00:02:28.584
"But what about Miss Bishop?

46
00:02:29.552 --> 00:02:30.852
She was sneaking around Mrs.

47
00:02:30.892 --> 00:02:32.133
Sweet's shed yesterday."

48
00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:34.413
"True," Cole said.

49
00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:37.554
"But she has no reason to want the parade cancelled.

50
00:02:38.414 --> 00:02:41.235
So she probably didn't post that threat on the website."

51
00:02:42.415 --> 00:02:44.236
"I guess you're right," Henry agreed.

52
00:02:44.256 --> 00:02:47.297
"That leaves one more suspect: Mr.

53
00:02:47.377 --> 00:02:49.657
Fleming." Maggie nodded.

54
00:02:49.677 --> 00:02:52.678
"He definitely wants the parade shut down."

55
00:02:52.698 --> 00:02:55.699
"But why would he steal Mrs.

56
00:02:55.759 --> 00:02:56.599
Sweet's candy?"

57
00:02:56.879 --> 00:02:57.639
Henry asked.

58
00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.160
"Who knows?"

59
00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.261
Cole grabbed a bottle of glue.

60
00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:05.242
"Let's finish our float and then go try to find out.

61
00:03:06.103 --> 00:03:09.444
We still have a few hours to investigate before the parade starts."

62
00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:17.987
An hour later The Lemonade Detectives waved to Maggie's dad as he drove away down the street on

63
00:03:18.007 --> 00:03:18.628
his tractor.

64
00:03:19.608 --> 00:03:21.329
The float was on the cart behind him.

65
00:03:22.309 --> 00:03:25.791
It was covered in a sheet so nobody would see it until the parade started.

66
00:03:25.811 --> 00:03:30.445
"I'll meet you kids at the high school at three o'clock," Maggie's dad said.

67
00:03:30.465 --> 00:03:33.306
"See you then," Henry called back.

68
00:03:33.326 --> 00:03:35.047
"Thanks, Uncle Bruce!"

69
00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:37.709
Henry and his friends walked to Mr.

70
00:03:37.749 --> 00:03:38.429
Fleming's house.

71
00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:44.772
A plump older woman was out in the yard watering some flowers.

72
00:03:44.792 --> 00:03:48.534
"That's his wife," Cole whispered to the others.

73
00:03:49.615 --> 00:03:50.836
Then he waved to the woman.

74
00:03:50.856 --> 00:03:51.996
"Hi, Mrs.

75
00:03:52.036 --> 00:03:55.118
Fleming!" "Oh, hello, Cole!"

76
00:03:55.778 --> 00:03:58.360
Mrs. Fleming put down her watering can and hurried over.

77
00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.113
"It's so nice to see you!

78
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:04.174
Are you excited for the parade this afternoon?"

79
00:04:04.194 --> 00:04:06.834
"Definitely," Cole said.

80
00:04:06.854 --> 00:04:12.176
"We heard your husband isn't very happy about the parade," Henry put in.

81
00:04:12.196 --> 00:04:16.417
"He thinks everyone is being too noisy building their floats."

82
00:04:17.418 --> 00:04:18.658
Mrs. Fleming sighed.

83
00:04:18.678 --> 00:04:20.179
"Yes, I know.

84
00:04:20.399 --> 00:04:22.239
He's been complaining all week.

85
00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.080
He hates noise.

86
00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:30.308
He's always yelling at the neighbors about their barking dogs or their loud lawn mowers."

87
00:04:31.309 --> 00:04:32.470
She smiled at the kids.

88
00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:34.932
"He's really a nice man, though.

89
00:04:35.633 --> 00:04:37.654
Too much noise just makes him cranky."

90
00:04:39.196 --> 00:04:40.296
Maggie stepped forward.

91
00:04:40.317 --> 00:04:45.461
"Do you think he was crabby enough to post a threatening message on the town website?"

92
00:04:45.721 --> 00:04:46.301
she asked.

93
00:04:47.402 --> 00:04:48.603
Mrs. Fleming chuckled.

94
00:04:48.623 --> 00:04:51.346
"Oh my, no," she said.

95
00:04:51.366 --> 00:04:53.848
"My husband hates computers.

96
00:04:54.636 --> 00:04:56.757
He won't touch one unless he has to.

97
00:04:57.737 --> 00:05:01.199
He even asks me to send emails to his clients for him."

98
00:05:01.219 --> 00:05:04.260
"Yes, that's true," Henry said.

99
00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.381
"Sorry to bother you, Mrs.

100
00:05:06.441 --> 00:05:09.442
Fleming." "It's no bother at all."

101
00:05:10.023 --> 00:05:11.903
Mrs. Fleming waved as they walked away.

102
00:05:11.923 --> 00:05:14.064
"Enjoy the parade, kids!"

103
00:05:14.084 --> 00:05:20.347
"She's a lot nicer than her husband," Maggie said as The Lemonade Detectives headed down the sidewalk.

104
00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:22.708
"Yeah," Henry said.

105
00:05:23.388 --> 00:05:24.548
"It sounds like Mr.

106
00:05:24.608 --> 00:05:26.029
Fleming isn't the culprit.

107
00:05:26.889 --> 00:05:31.150
He hates computers, so he probably wouldn't have posted that threat."

108
00:05:31.971 --> 00:05:32.751
Cole nodded.

109
00:05:32.771 --> 00:05:36.292
"Plus, it's hard to imagine him breaking into Mrs.

110
00:05:36.352 --> 00:05:37.132
Sweet's shed.

111
00:05:38.112 --> 00:05:39.653
So who should we investigate next?"

112
00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:41.934
"How about Jackson?"

113
00:05:42.114 --> 00:05:43.074
Henry suggested.

114
00:05:43.094 --> 00:05:46.655
"Let's go to the newspaper office and see if he's there."

115
00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:53.902
Soon they reached the office.

116
00:05:54.984 --> 00:05:57.548
"I'm sorry, kids," the receptionist told them.

117
00:05:57.568 --> 00:05:59.371
"Jackson isn't here.

118
00:06:00.453 --> 00:06:01.634
He just rushed out.

119
00:06:02.155 --> 00:06:06.262
He said there's some urgent breaking news that will make the newspaper's front page!"
